[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066] STEP PURPOSE
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   step_066: Secular stability of the real detached-TNO cluster under
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   the measured planetary system, with and without the published
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   Planet Nine.
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   The shepherding hypothesis requires the observed varpi alignment to be
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   *maintained*: differential apsidal precession under the known planets
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   otherwise disperses the cluster on a measurable timescale.  This step
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   integrates the actual catalogued population -- the 44 detached TNOs
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   (a > 150 AU, q > 30 AU, condition code <= 3; identical selection to
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   step_010) -- forward through the real planetary system (Sun + giant
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   planets on DE440s states) and measures the apsidal-precession rates
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   directly.
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   Three realizations are compared:
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   giants        : Sun + Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, Neptune (DE440s)
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   giants+bb21ml : + Brown & Batygin (2021) maximum-likelihood Planet Nine
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   (m9=5.0 M_E, a9=300 AU, e9=0.15, i9=17 deg,
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   varpi9=254 deg, Om9=108 deg, M9=0)
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   giants+bb21med: + BB21 marginalized-median model
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   (m9=6.9 M_E, a9=461 AU, e9=0.30, i9=15.6 deg,
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   varpi9=246.7 deg, Om9=96.9 deg, M9=0)
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   The TNOs are massless test particles started from their catalogued
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   osculating elements at a common epoch (median element epoch; along-track
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   phase is drawn uniformly since SBDB supplies no mean anomaly -- apsidal
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   precession is phase-independent).
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   Measured per object over the integration:
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   dvarpi/dt   : linear drift of the longitude of perihelion -> the
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   differential-precession dispersal rate
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   Dvarpi(t)   : varpi relative to P9's varpi -- the libration coordinate
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   a confining perturber must hold near 180 deg
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   Reported:
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   sigma(dvarpi/dt) per model -> dispersal time t_disp = sigma_varpi /
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   sigma(dvarpi/dt) for the observed cluster spread;
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   the P9 restoring signature: correlation of the P9-added drift
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   dvarpi_P9 - dvarpi_giants against the offset (Dvarpi - 180 deg);
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   R_varpi(t) of the observed cluster under each model.
[2026-09-21 14:41:43 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 066]   Outputs
